From b8d5297c274625c66908dc675d4667547c9104ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ayush Chaurasia <ayush@lancedb.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 21:44:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(v1): durable artifact sink for collected outputs (#2189)

collect() retains every tar archive on trace.state.artifacts, which is
excluded from serialization -- so artifacts cost host RAM for the life of
the trace and cannot be inspected after a run. This adds an optional sink
that moves each archive to durable storage as it is collected and leaves a
self-describing ArtifactRef in its place; restore() fetches referenced
archives back on demand, digest-verified.

- new verifiers/v1/utils/artifact_sink.py: ArtifactRef, ArtifactSink ABC
  (async put/get), DirectorySink (per-trace tars + manifest.json, atomic
  writes, sha256 verification), load_sink(spec) (directory path, or a
  pkg.module:factory?args plugin returning a custom sink)
- collect() gains optional sink/trace_id kwargs; with a sink, values are
  ArtifactRefs and nothing is retained in memory. Default path (no sink) is
  byte-for-byte unchanged. Writes shielded like episode output.
- restore() dereferences ArtifactRefs before extraction
- State.artifacts widens to dict[str, bytes | ArtifactRef | None]
- TaskConfig.artifact_sink knob (--env.taskset.task.artifact-sink)
- docs/v1/harbor.md documents the option

Addresses the follow-up scope of #2189: a host-side artifact sink with a
manifest and per-source status, streaming to storage instead of retaining
payloads in Trace.state, inspectable after eval. External stores (e.g. a
columnar/object-store backend) plug in via load_sink without further changes.

